# Project Tech Stack
- Next.js (App Router ONLY)
- React 19 (Server Components by default)
- TypeScript (Strict mode, NEVER use 'any')
- Tailwind CSS & Shadcn UI
- Supabase (PostgreSQL, strict RLS)

# Code Generation Rules (CRITICAL)
1. NO LEGACY: Do not use class components, `useEffect` for data fetching (use Server Components or SWR/React Query), or Next.js Pages router conventions.
2. SERVER FIRST: Assume components are React Server Components (RSC) unless interactivity (hooks, events) is required. Use `"use client"` ONLY when absolutely necessary.
3. SUPABASE SECURITY: Never bypass RLS. Do not use service_role keys in the client. All direct DB mutations must happen via Next.js Server Actions.
4. DIFFING FORMAT: When modifying a file, DO NOT output the entire file if it's large. Output the exact `import` statements (if changed) and the FULL, complete function/component block being modified. Do not use `// ... rest of function` inside the modified block. Cursor Apply must be able to replace the whole block cleanly.
5. CLEAN CODE: Keep functions small. Use early returns. Name variables descriptively. Remove console.logs before final output.
6. CONTEXT AWARENESS: Before writing new utility functions or UI components, check if they already exist in `@/src/lib/` or `@/src/components/ui/` to avoid duplication.